----- stdout -----
Measure where each instruction's compute units go, line by line.

Builds the program with DWARF line tables, runs its Mollusk tests with register tracing, and attributes every executed SBF instruction to a source line and call stack. Prints a summary per traced instruction and writes a self-contained HTML report to <target>/pina/trace/<program>.html. The program's mollusk-svm dev-dependency must enable the `register-tracing` feature.

Usage: pina profile trace [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --project <DIR>
          Directory inside the project to discover

      --filter <TEST>
          Run only tests whose names contain TEST (passed to `cargo test`)

      --instruction <NAME>
          Report only this instruction (any case style, or a label such as `increment #2`)

      --trace-dir <DIR>
          Analyze existing traces in DIR instead of building and running tests.
          
          Attribution uses the traced build from the project's last `pina profile trace`.

      --json
          Emit the versioned JSON document instead of the text summary

      --folded
          Emit Brendan Gregg folded stacks for speedscope, inferno, or flamegraph.pl

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Write the selected output to FILE instead of stdout

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  pina profile trace
  pina profile trace --project ./programs/counter_program
  pina profile trace --filter increment --instruction increment
  pina profile trace --json -o ./trace.json
  pina profile trace --folded > ./stacks.folded
  pina profile trace --trace-dir ./target/pina/trace/traces

Cost model:
  Every executed SBF instruction costs 1 CU. The runtime charges syscalls separately; they are listed by name and call site but their charges are not included.

Setup:
  Enable tracing in the program's Cargo.toml:
    [dev-dependencies]
    mollusk-svm = { version = "0.15", features = ["register-tracing"] }

